-- title:
--   Units at the two fibre generic points: Q(j) for ̄ Q≠ 0
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5\le p$ and a Deligne–Rapoport package $\mathfrak X$ at $p$, i.e. a term of `DRModelPackage p`, whose data consist of: the properness, flatness and integrality of the structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak D =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ (modularFunctionFieldFull p) (IgusaScheme.jFull p)` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, integral closedness of the sections over every affine open, a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb Q$ and a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for the relevant modular function fields together with isomorphisms onto the corresponding base changes of $\mathfrak D$ and the stated Galois equivariance and compatibility of the associated places, two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ of `DRModel.toBase p`, a distinguished open (the smooth locus) with its relative dimension and maximality properties, and the further fields of the structure, among them the family `𝔛.ratModel`, `𝔛.compInf` and `𝔛.compZero` used below.
--
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, and let `hϖ` be the hypothesis that its maximal ideal is generated by $p$; the base change $\mathfrak X_O := \mathfrak D\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z}\operatorname{Spec}O$, formed as the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z\to O$, is assumed integral (`hint`). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O\to k$ a ring homomorphism; `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` denotes the induced morphism $\mathfrak X_k\to\mathfrak X_O$, obtained from the identity on $\mathfrak D$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{to}\kappa$.
--
--   Write $U\subseteq\mathfrak X_O$ for the preimage under the first projection $\mathfrak X_O\to\mathfrak D$ of the open image of the finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$, and let $J\in K(\mathfrak X_O)$ be the image in the function field, under `germToFunctionField` on $U$, of the pullback to $U$ of the chart element `TwoChartIntegralModel.jChartFin` (the element $j$ of the finite chart algebra, transported along the isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A)\cong A$ and the open immersion $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$). The hypothesis `hne` asserts that $U$ is nonempty.
--
--   Let $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ be the points of $\mathfrak X_O$ obtained by applying the underlying maps of `𝔛.compInf k` followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, respectively `𝔛.compZero k` followed by the same morphism, to the generic point of the scheme $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_O$, membership in the range of the canonical map $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,x}\to K(\mathfrak X_O)$ is the assertion that the given rational function is regular at $x$. The two remaining hypotheses are that $J$ lies in the image of the stalk at $\xi_\infty$ (`hJinf`) and that $J$ lies in the image of the stalk at $\xi_0$ (`hJzero`).
--
--   Under these assumptions the conclusion is: for every $Q\in\mathbb Z[X]$ whose reduction along $\mathbb Z\to\mathbb Z/p$ is nonzero, writing $Q(J) :=$ `Polynomial.eval₂` of the structure map $\mathbb Z\to K(\mathfrak X_O)$ at $J$ applied to $Q$, the following four statements hold, grouped in the Lean as a conjunction of two pairs: $Q(J)$ lies in the image of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,\xi_\infty}$ in $K(\mathfrak X_O)$; $Q(J)^{-1}$ lies in the image of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,\xi_\infty}$; $Q(J)$ lies in the image of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,\xi_0}$; and $Q(J)^{-1}$ lies in the image of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X_O,\xi_0}$. Equivalently, $Q(J)$ is a unit of each of the two local rings, viewed inside the function field.
--
--   This is the regularity-and-invertibility statement expressing that the modular function $j$ is transcendental along each of the two labelled components of the mod $p$ fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model base changed to an unramified discrete valuation ring: any integral polynomial in $j$ with nonzero reduction modulo $p$ is a unit at both generic points. It is used by the two lemmas [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.phi_algebraMap_stalk_mem_integers_and_exists_eq_jFun_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.phi_algebraMap_stalk_mem_integers_and_exists_eq_jFun_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal) and its `_swap` variant, which identify the local rings at these points with valuation rings of the modular function field.
